From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Fri, 04 Apr 2026 11:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: arm: compressed: sun5i AHB/MBUS settle before kernel entry

On Allwinner sun5i (R8/A13, C.H.I.P.) the zImage decompressor writes
~15 MiB of decompressed kernel data to DRAM in one continuous burst.
cache_clean_flush() then flushes all dirty D-cache lines to DRAM,
adding another large write burst.

When the decompressor jumps to the decompressed kernel at r4, the
first instruction fetch from that address stalls the CPU indefinitely:
the AHB/MBUS bus arbiter has not drained the write transactions.

Fix: in __enter_kernel, immediately before the branch to r4, issue a
DSB + busy-wait loop long enough to drain the arbiter (~200 ms at
1 GHz, the nominal R8 clock frequency).

  mcr p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4   @ ARMv5 DSB (CP15 write-buffer drain)
  0x04000000 = 67,108,864 iters * ~3 cycles/iter @ 1 GHz ≈ 200 ms

Guarded by CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I so it only fires on affected silicon.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -1432,6 +1432,23 @@
 #endif /* CONFIG_ARM_VIRT_EXT */
 
 __enter_kernel:
+#ifdef CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I
+		/*
+		 * sun5i (R8/A13) AHB/MBUS bus stall.
+		 * cache_clean_flush() just flushed ~15 MiB of decompressed
+		 * kernel data to DRAM.  The AHB arbiter retains those write
+		 * transactions; the first instruction fetch from the
+		 * decompressed kernel at r4 stalls the CPU indefinitely.
+		 * DSB + ~200 ms busy-wait drains the arbiter before the jump.
+		 * 0x04000000 = 67,108,864 iters; at ~3 cycles/iter on ARM926
+		 * @ 1 GHz ≈ 200 ms.
+		 */
+		mcr	p15, 0, r0, c7, c10, 4		@ DSB
+		mov	r3, #0x04000000			@ ~67M iters ≈ 200ms @ 1GHz
+sun5i_settle:
+		subs	r3, r3, #1
+		bne	sun5i_settle
+#endif
 		mov	r0, #0			@ must be 0
 		mov	r1, r7			@ restore architecture number
 		mov	r2, r8			@ restore atags pointer
